thin-slice "TS.260820.14" {
    slug "record-a-decision"
    title "Bind a decision to the work that forced it, and correct it only by appending"
    kind "command"
    realizes "CAP.claim-settlement"
    from-storm "ES.260819.01"

    command "record-decision"
    actor "working-agent"
    produces-event "DecisionRecorded"
    needs-read-model "the-decisions-that-shaped-this"
    feeds-read-model "the-decisions-that-shaped-this"

    trigger "an iteration hits a choice it cannot make implicitly"
    outcome "the decision exists, attached to the iteration that forced it, with what it rejected and what will test it"

    scenario #"""
        Given an iteration that must choose between real alternatives
        When the agent records the decision
        Then it is bound to that iteration, carries the alternatives it rejected, and names what
             would show it wrong — and once accepted it is corrected only by APPENDING an
             amendment, never by rewriting, because a decision that can be edited afterwards
             is a decision nobody can cite.
        """#

    step "1" does="state the choice, and the alternatives that were genuinely available"
    step "2" does="bind it to the iteration that forced it, not to a folder beside the work"
    step "3" does="name what would falsify it — a decision with no falsifier is a preference"
    step "4" does="on later correction, append an amendment naming what changed and why. The original stays readable"

    excludes "rewriting an accepted decision, at any point, for any reason"
    excludes "deciding whether the decision was good. Findings test it; this slice records it"
    excludes "discovery-time rejected options. Those belong to the frame's discovery and reach a \
        reader through the same composite document (ES.260819.01/E23)"

    layer "doctrine"    reaches="the skill teaches append-only correction and the falsifier requirement"
    layer "enforcement" reaches="an edit to an accepted decision's body is refused; an amendment is not"
    layer "docs"        reaches="published under docs/releases/<version>/decisions/, composed with the options discovery rejected"

    claim "C1" text="editing the body of an accepted decision is refused; appending an amendment is not" \
        settled-by="a negative test mutating an accepted body, and a positive test appending an amendment"
    claim "C2" text="a decision with no alternatives and no falsifier is refused" \
        settled-by="two negative tests, one per missing field"
    claim "C3" text="a decision not bound to an iteration is refused" \
        settled-by="a negative test with a dangling iteration reference"
    claim "C4" text="findings that tested a decision are reachable from it" \
        settled-by="a test asserting the traversal from a decision to the findings raised against it"

    depends-on "TS.260820.05 — a decision binds to an iteration, so an iteration must be open"

    useful-alone "a reader stops asking why something is the way it is and getting an answer \
        reconstructed from memory. Worth having with nothing published at all"

    attacks "S2" "S7"
    note "the composite decision document is E19's second use: this capability carries the decision, \
        its amendments and the findings that tested it; delivery-record carries what discovery rejected"
}
